{"model": "gpt-oss-120b", "input": [{"role": "developer", "content": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "Repair previous_candidate, the complete immediately preceding candidate bound to candidate_version and candidate_sha256. Return the entire revision in one <BEGIN_SHACL> ... <END_SHACL> block. No fresh regeneration. Use current_findings and the supplied evidence catalog. Deterministic diagnostics are preserved exactly; full model-review responses remain artifacts, not independent proof or repair permissions.\n\nCorrect supported defects while preserving source obligations, numeric comparisons, units, datatypes, targets, paths and conditional branches. Correct identifiers from explicit declarations; never remove constraints merely to silence a canonical-identifier error. Unit renaming is not numeric conversion. An old constraint may be excessive: supported removal is allowed but will require source-grounded change/removal assessment and prior-issue reconciliation on recheck.\n\nSource/schema evidence is supplied once with local IDs mapped to immutable provenance. Missing references, unknown ownership or material uncertainty must remain unresolved; do not invent facts, conversions or applicability. Ontology domain/range does not establish exclusive ownership or legal eligibility. The common caller declaration states the research population and selected editions, not certified real-vessel eligibility. Never request evaluation identities, labels, counterparts or reference solutions. Conditions within the represented requirement remain in scope. A successful execution-only probe does not establish regulatory correctness or full branch coverage.\n"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "{\"requirement_id\": \"IMO-001\", \"candidate_version\": 1, \"candidate_sha256\": \"13a44ed99215297e9d2b37b544ed99652253fa16e6ebfad587ba2dbd6a3ec419\", \"previous_candidate\": \"@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\\n\\n# Shape representing the regulatory definition of a Category A ship\\n# Source: IMO‑001 “2.1 Category A ship means a ship designed for operation in polar waters in at least medium first‑year ice, which may include old ice inclusions.”\\n# The admission declares the complete synthetic population of nltl:ship instances.\\n\\n:CategoryAShipShape\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\\n    rdfs:label \\\"Category A ship shape\\\" ;\\n    rdfs:comment \\\"Enforces that a ship classified as Category A has the required design ice condition per IMO‑001 §2.1.\\\" ;\\n    \\n    # Ship must be assigned the Category A value\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path nltl:shipCategory ;\\n        sh:hasValue nltl:polarShipCategoryA ;\\n        sh:severity sh:Info ;\\n        sh:message \\\"Ship is classified as Category A (polarShipCategoryA).\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    \\n    # Design ice condition must be at least medium first‑year ice with possible old‑ice inclusions\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path nltl:designIceCondition ;\\n        sh:hasValue nltl:mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions ;\\n        sh:severity sh:Violation ;\\n        sh:message \\\"Category A ship must be designed for operation in at least medium first‑year ice (may include old ice inclusions).\\\" ;\\n    ] .\\n\", \"current_findings\": [{\"category\": \"PARSE_ERROR\", \"message\": \"Turtle parse failed\", \"location\": \"Turtle parser line 11 [line 11, column 1]\", \"expected\": \"\", \"evidence\": \"rdflib Turtle parser\", \"suggestion\": \"Correct only the reported syntax.\", \"version\": 1, \"candidate_sha256\": \"13a44ed99215297e9d2b37b544ed99652253fa16e6ebfad587ba2dbd6a3ec419\", \"diagnostic\": \"at line 11 of <>:\\nBad syntax (Prefix \\\":\\\" not bound) at ^ in:\\n\\\"...b'ion declares the complete synthetic population of nltl:ship '^b'instances.\\\\n\\\\n:CategoryAShipShape\\\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\\\n    sh:'...\\\"\", \"confirmed\": true, \"contract_id\": \"candidate-structural\", \"obligation_id\": \"PARSE_ERROR\", \"check_id\": \"9b8724196e896b88ff63952700dea25c9552b7e0211ddb193f879c567f6f76a5\", \"query_sha256\": \"\", \"assessment\": \"CONFIRMED_FINDING\", \"blocking\": true, \"candidate_location\": {\"candidate_version\": 1, \"candidate_sha256\": \"13a44ed99215297e9d2b37b544ed99652253fa16e6ebfad587ba2dbd6a3ec419\", \"unit\": \"characters\", \"start\": 577, \"end\": 596}}], \"protocol_version\": 2, \"context\": {\"requirement\": {\"id\": \"IMO-001\", \"source\": \"International Code for Ships Operating in Polar Waters (Polar Code)\", \"clause\": \"Introduction 2.1\"}, \"scope\": \"Implement and review the supplied source in the declared schema. No supplied compliance solution or expected verdict. Material unspecified representation/applicability prevents acceptance. External population/date eligibility and edition selection are supplied by caller admission, not independently inferred from RDF. Conditions within the represented requirement remain in scope; activation and query correctness are separate obligations.\", \"source_selection\": {\"manifest_sha256\": \"5107d6c3ab2e5bf2a719d18bc929cddcaf2d500a3c773c04e4be52a6fd4540ad\", \"included_characters\": 10966, \"original_characters\": 143581, \"omitted_sections\": 395, \"retrieval\": \"Schema.source_evidence(file, document_sha256, start, end); complete sections/hashes retained in source_selection_manifest.json; missing necessary evidence must remain unresolved\"}, \"source_completeness\": \"Deterministic source selection, not a proof of complete context. Ambiguous primary anchors retain full source; unresolved references require review.\"}, \"evidence_catalog\": {\"format_version\": 2, \"catalog_sha256\": \"0e7e9136987f95f3cc0492dea3c26edbd487ea4fcf0280cd5d989be5c0ff6c56\", \"entries\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"E1\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-0676\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E2\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceConditionValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Ice condition value\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E3\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#thinFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"NamedIndividual\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Thin first-year ice with possible old-ice inclusions\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"thinFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceConditionValue\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"IMO-002\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E4\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#otherWatersIceCondition> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO-102\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E5\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#otherWatersIceCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (R9 development): Other waters ice condition represents the linked requirement entity, relationship, value, evidence role, or quantity; its scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E6\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designIceCondition\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"ObjectProperty\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Design ice condition\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"designIceCondition\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceConditionValue\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"IMO-001 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.9 | 2.1; IMO-002 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.9 | 2.2; IMO-003 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.9 | 2.3\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E7\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#polarShipCategoryB\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"NamedIndividual\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Category B\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"polarShipCategoryB\\\", \\\"mapping_basis\\\": \\\"Ontology declaration (registry row not required)\\\", \\\"types\\\": [\\\"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#polarShipCategoryValue\\\"]}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E8\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designIceCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Design ice condition\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E9\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#polarShipCategoryValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"IMO polar ship category value\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E10\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceReference> \\\"IMO26-002 | IMO_AMEND_2026 p.2 | Chapter 9-1 applicability; IMO26-016 | IMO_AMEND_2026 p.5 | Chapter 11-1 applicability\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E11\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Ship category\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E12\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designIceCondition> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Locked-workbook normalized regulatory term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E13\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"4.1      Definitions\\n\\n4.1.1   Constructed means a ship the keel of which is laid or which is at a similar stage of\\nconstruction.\\n\\n4.1.2  Ice-shelf means a floating ice sheet of considerable thickness, showing 2 to 50 m or\\nmore above sea-level, attached to the coast.\\n\\n4.1.3   Fast ice means sea ice which forms and remains fast along the coast, where it is\\nattached to the shore, to an ice wall, to an ice front, between shoals or grounded icebergs.\\n\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/IMO_full.txt\", \"authority\": \"User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 101992, \"end\": 102443}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E14\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#polarShipCategoryA> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E15\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E16\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Benchmark entity\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E17\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO-108\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E18\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#fishingVessel> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E19\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitDecisionStatus> \\\"Not a quantity property\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E20\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO26-016\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E21\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#fishingVessel> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-0270\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E22\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#cargoShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#stage1LocalName> \\\"cargoShip\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E23\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO-110\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E24\", \"kind\": \"CONTEXT_STATUS\", \"text\": \"[]\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"unresolvedOwnership\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E25\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#polarShipCategoryA> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#polarShipCategoryValue> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E26\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceFreeIceCondition\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"NamedIndividual\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Ice free ice condition\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"iceFreeIceCondition\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceConditionValue\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"IMO-102 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.30 | 12.3.1\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E27\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#thinFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Thin first-year ice with possible old-ice inclusions\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E28\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#cargoShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO26-016\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E29\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceConditionValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E30\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#oilTanker> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#evidenceExcerpt> \\\"For category A and B ships other than oil tankers constructed on or after 1 January 2017, all cargo tanks constructed and utilized to carry oil shall be separated from the outer shell by a distance of not less than 0.76 m.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E31\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO-002\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E32\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO-111\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E33\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceConditionValue\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"Class\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Ice condition value\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"iceConditionValue\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"IMO-007 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.9 | 2.10; IMO-102 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.30 | 12.3.1\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E34\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Pleasure yacht\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E35\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceConditionLessSevereThanCategoryAAndB> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Ice condition less severe than categories A and B\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E36\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E37\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceFreeIceCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Ice free ice condition\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E38\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-R7-0005\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E39\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designIceCondition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E40\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceFreeIceCondition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E41\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO-114\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E42\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceConditionLessSevereThanCategoryAAndB> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-R7-0006\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E43\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#cargoShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E44\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#polarShipCategoryValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E45\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#oilTanker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Oil tanker\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E46\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for passengerShip derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E47\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"4       INVITES ALSO Contracting Governments to consider the voluntary application of\\nthe Polar Code, as far as practicable, also to ships not covered by the Polar Code and\\noperating in polar waters;\\n\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/IMO_full.txt\", \"authority\": \"User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 2385, \"end\": 2586}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E48\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designIceCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> \\\"design_ice_condition\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E49\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#fishingVessel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Fishing vessel\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E50\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceConditionValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Ice condition value\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E51\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E52\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E53\", \"kind\": \"CONTEXT_STATUS\", \"text\": \"[]\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"unresolvedSourceContext\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E54\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#polarShipCategoryB> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E55\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"4.6      The process includes the following stages of assessment:\\n\\n         .1       select the target Polar Class for equivalency;\\n\\n         .2       compare materials used in the design with minimum requirements under\\n                  the IACS Polar Class URs; identify any shortfalls; and\\n\\n         .3       compare strength levels of hull and machinery components design with\\n                  requirements under the IACS Polar Class URs; quantify levels of compliance.\\n\\n         Where gaps in compliance are identified in steps 1 to 3, additional steps should be\\n         necessary to demonstrate equivalency, as outlined below:\\n\\n         .4       identify any risk mitigation measures incorporated in the design of the ship\\n                  (over and above the requirements of the Code and IACS URs);\\n\\n         .5       where applicable, provide documentation of service experience of existing\\n                  ships, in conditions relevant to the target ice class for equivalency; and\\n\\n         .6       undertake an assessment, taking into account information from steps 1 to 5,\\n                  as applicable, and the principles outlined in paragraphs 4.2 to 4.6 above.\\n\\n4.7      Documentation provided with an application for equivalency should identify each\\nstage that has been undertaken, and sufficient supporting information to validate assessments.\\n\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/IMO_full.txt\", \"authority\": \"User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 86885, \"end\": 88254}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E56\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"Class\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Passenger ship\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"passengerShip\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"IMO-070 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.24 | 8.3.3.1.1; IMO-118 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.43 | 4.2.2\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E57\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E58\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#cargoShip> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E59\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E60\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Passenger ship\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E61\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#thinFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Thin first-year ice with possible old-ice inclusions\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E62\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#stage1LocalName> \\\"passengerShip\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E63\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designIceCondition> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO-002\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E64\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E65\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Locked-workbook normalized regulatory term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E66\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitDecisionStatus> \\\"Not a quantity property\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E67\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#polarShipCategoryC> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E68\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceConditionValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E69\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#evidenceExcerpt> \\\"Category A ship means a ship designed for operation in polar waters in at least medium first-year ice, which may include old ice inclusions.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E70\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#fishingVessel> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO26-002\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E71\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#module> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleMachinery> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E72\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#otherWatersIceCondition> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-R13-0006\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E73\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E74\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#thinFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-R11-0008\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E75\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#oilTanker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E76\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#otherWatersIceCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Other waters ice condition\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E77\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"4.3     The scope of a simplified equivalency assessment (see paragraph 4.6 below) is\\nexpected to be limited to materials selection, structural strength of the hull and propulsion\\nmachinery.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n      Refer to the Guidelines for the approval of alternatives and equivalents as provided for in various IMO\\n      instruments (MSC.1/Circ.1455).\\n†\\n      Refer to the annex to HELCOM Recommendation 25/7, Safety of Winter Navigation in the Baltic Sea Area,\\n      available at www.helcom.fi\\n\\f                         RESOLUTION MSC.385(94) (adopted on 21 November 2014)\\n                     INTERNATIONAL CODE FOR SHIPS OPERATING IN POLAR WATERS\\n                                          (POLAR CODE)\\n\\n                                               - 35 -\\n\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/IMO_full.txt\", \"authority\": \"User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 84982, \"end\": 85735}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E78\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> \\\"passenger_ship\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E79\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"declaration_evidence\\\": {\\\"numericValue\\\": {\\\"@id\\\": \\\"qudt:numericValue\\\", \\\"@type\\\": \\\"xsd:decimal\\\"}, \\\"unit\\\": {\\\"@id\\\": \\\"qudt:unit\\\", \\\"@type\\\": \\\"@id\\\"}}, \\\"iri\\\": \\\"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"ObjectProperty\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"unit\\\", \\\"mapping_basis\\\": \\\"Declared JSON-LD schema/locked_representation_context.jsonld\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E80\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#cargoShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO26-002\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E81\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipCategory> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingRule> \\\"N4 - preserve the source concept; normalize spelling to ASCII lowerCamelCase\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E82\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#evidenceExcerpt> \\\"This chapter applies to: fishing vessels of 24 metres in length overall and above; pleasure yachts of 300 gross tonnage and upwards not engaged in trade; and cargo ships of 300 gross tonnage and upwards but below 500 gross tonnage.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E83\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-0528\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E84\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designIceCondition> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#module> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleCore> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E85\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#fishingVessel> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO26-016\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E86\", \"kind\": \"CALLER_DECLARATION\", \"text\": \"{\\\"declaration\\\": {\\\"admission_id\\\": \\\"SYNTHETIC_DESIGN_RESEARCH_SCOPE_IMO_001_V1\\\", \\\"approval\\\": {\\\"approved_by\\\": \\\"User in the current conversation\\\", \\\"reference\\\": \\\"User instruction in the current conversation, 2026-11-24 (verbatim approval):\\\\nI approve the grouped synthetic research-scope proposal and its\\\\nexperimental edition selections for I2-005, IMO-001, TRF-010 and\\\\nTRF-035. I approve TRF-035 option A: recorded ruleLength and a\\\\nseparately supplied classificationSocietyRuleLength reference datum.\\\\n\\\\nRecord this instruction as approval provenance. Retain the stated\\\\nlimits: research assumptions do not certify real-vessel eligibility,\\\\nlegal governing editions or society-rule derivation.\\\\n\\\\nPreserve every generated candidate, including the last rejected one,\\\\nwith its findings and terminal reason. Keep acceptance criteria\\\\nidentical across attempts. Do not add a lenient final attempt,\\\\nfallback acceptance or human-review arm.\\\\n\\\\nSelected NLTL output remains the first internally accepted candidate.\\\\nIf none is accepted, report NO_VERDICT. Evaluate rejected candidates\\\\nonly as separately labelled diagnostics; never select by external score.\\\\n\\\\nFinalize the five-requirement paired pilot manifest using the approved\\\\nscopes and TRF-035 mapping choice. Verify identical actual initial\\\\nrequests/settings across arms, evaluation isolation and the existing\\\\n55-call maximum with early stopping.\\\\n\\\\nKeep v0.10.1 implementation frozen. No further pipeline changes.\\\\nReturn final readiness and exact dispatch instructions.\\\\nDo not make model calls or dispatch yet.\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"APPROVED\\\"}, \\\"eligibility_assertion\\\": \\\"ASSUMED_EXTERNAL_RESEARCH_ELIGIBILITY\\\", \\\"focus_set\\\": {\\\"mode\\\": \\\"COMPLETE_CLASS_POPULATION_PER_INPUT\\\", \\\"owner_class\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship\\\"}, \\\"format_version\\\": 2, \\\"interpretation\\\": \\\"A\\\", \\\"population_description\\\": \\\"Synthetic ship-design records supplied as the complete nltl:ship population of each input. External legal/application eligibility and the experimental source-edition selection are research assumptions, not facts inferred from RDF. This is not real-vessel certification. The population includes incomplete, inconsistent and unrecognized-value records; represented correctness is not assumed. Conditions inside the represented requirement, effective activation, missing represented inputs, paths, units, datatypes and query correctness remain for generated SHACL to address from supplied source/schema. The represented domain is Polar Code Introduction 2.1 design-condition/category records externally assumed within the selected safety-related Code research population. The supplied controlled design-condition value is a record of design intent, not independently measured ice-navigation capability. No particular category or design condition is assumed true for every record; source conditions and unavailable selector information remain generated-validation/review responsibilities.\\\", \\\"provenance\\\": {\\\"basis\\\": \\\"User-approved grouped synthetic research assumptions and experimental editions; no certification of real-vessel eligibility, governing legal editions or society-rule derivation.\\\", \\\"declarant\\\": \\\"User in the current conversation\\\", \\\"reference\\\": \\\"User instruction in the current conversation, 2026-11-24 (verbatim approval):\\\\nI approve the grouped synthetic research-scope proposal and its\\\\nexperimental edition selections for I2-005, IMO-001, TRF-010 and\\\\nTRF-035. I approve TRF-035 option A: recorded ruleLength and a\\\\nseparately supplied classificationSocietyRuleLength reference datum.\\\\n\\\\nRecord this instruction as approval provenance. Retain the stated\\\\nlimits: research assumptions do not certify real-vessel eligibility,\\\\nlegal governing editions or society-rule derivation.\\\\n\\\\nPreserve every generated candidate, including the last rejected one,\\\\nwith its findings and terminal reason. Keep acceptance criteria\\\\nidentical across attempts. Do not add a lenient final attempt,\\\\nfallback acceptance or human-review arm.\\\\n\\\\nSelected NLTL output remains the first internally accepted candidate.\\\\nIf none is accepted, report NO_VERDICT. Evaluate rejected candidates\\\\nonly as separately labelled diagnostics; never select by external score.\\\\n\\\\nFinalize the five-requirement paired pilot manifest using the approved\\\\nscopes and TRF-035 mapping choice. Verify identical actual initial\\\\nrequests/settings across arms, evaluation isolation and the existing\\\\n55-call maximum with early stopping.\\\\n\\\\nKeep v0.10.1 implementation frozen. No further pipeline changes.\\\\nReturn final readiness and exact dispatch instructions.\\\\nDo not make model calls or dispatch yet.\\\"}, \\\"source_editions\\\": [{\\\"document_id\\\": \\\"MSC.385(94)\\\", \\\"edition\\\": \\\"Resolution MSC.385(94) (adopted 21 November 2014)\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"data/requirements/IMO_full.txt\\\", \\\"selection_provenance\\\": \\\"User instruction in the current conversation, 2026-11-24 (verbatim approval):\\\\nI approve the grouped synthetic research-scope proposal and its\\\\nexperimental edition selections for I2-005, IMO-001, TRF-010 and\\\\nTRF-035. I approve TRF-035 option A: recorded ruleLength and a\\\\nseparately supplied classificationSocietyRuleLength reference datum.\\\\n\\\\nRecord this instruction as approval provenance. Retain the stated\\\\nlimits: research assumptions do not certify real-vessel eligibility,\\\\nlegal governing editions or society-rule derivation.\\\\n\\\\nPreserve every generated candidate, including the last rejected one,\\\\nwith its findings and terminal reason. Keep acceptance criteria\\\\nidentical across attempts. Do not add a lenient final attempt,\\\\nfallback acceptance or human-review arm.\\\\n\\\\nSelected NLTL output remains the first internally accepted candidate.\\\\nIf none is accepted, report NO_VERDICT. Evaluate rejected candidates\\\\nonly as separately labelled diagnostics; never select by external score.\\\\n\\\\nFinalize the five-requirement paired pilot manifest using the approved\\\\nscopes and TRF-035 mapping choice. Verify identical actual initial\\\\nrequests/settings across arms, evaluation isolation and the existing\\\\n55-call maximum with early stopping.\\\\n\\\\nKeep v0.10.1 implementation frozen. No further pipeline changes.\\\\nReturn final readiness and exact dispatch instructions.\\\\nDo not make model calls or dispatch yet.\\\\nExperimental source selection only, not legally governing-edition determination.\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"27ffb65eeae2519755523f40105ea0611d4f8238f15dddb7b46